{
  "id": "finite-symmetric-tensor-categories-and-the-verlinde-tower",
  "title": "Finite symmetric tensor categories and the Verlinde tower",
  "description": "Every finite symmetric tensor category in characteristic p > 0 admits a fibre functor to a higher Verlinde category, the finite case of the Benson-Etingof-Ostrik conjecture, after OpenAI's 2026 manuscript. Tilting modules for SL_2; an equivariant vector bundle on the plane and the restricted tilting theorem; higher Frobenius functors; norm maps and symmetrizers; rank varieties; descent through Frobenius-Perron dimensions; incompressible categories and reconstruction.",
